  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The latest version of the VRC SDK for Unity has added an auto-line-break feature when pressing Enter while entering usernames and passwords. However, because my input method is not native English, every time I need to type a lowercase letter, I have to press Enter to confirm it. Due to the auto-line-break feature, pressing Enter automatically triggers the login process. This forces me to dismiss the incorrect password error popup with OK, then click back into the password field with the mouse to continue typing the rest of my password. While the auto-line-break on Enter might save a tiny bit of time, trust me, it is extremely unfriendly to many non-English input methods, and many users actually end up wasting more time because of it. I hope you can remove the newly added auto-line-break on Enter feature, or add an option that lets users disable it.For details, please refer to the video file attached to the request.",
